\subsection{Finding missing assignments}

For disjunctive maximum grading, the semantics of \enquote{missing} are
fundamentally different from conjunctive modules.
Since a student only needs ONE passing grade to pass the group:
\begin{itemize}
\item If the student has at least one passing grade, \emph{nothing} is missing.
\item If the student has no passing grades, we report \emph{all} assignments
  as options they could complete to pass.
\end{itemize}

This is in contrast to conjunctive modules (like [[conjunctavg]]), where each
non-passing assignment is independently \enquote{missing}.

We cannot reuse the shared implementation from [[canvaslms.cli.results]] because
that iterates assignment-by-assignment.
Disjunctive logic requires evaluating ALL assignments first, then deciding what
to report.

Surveys follow the opposite, conjunctive rule, as in [[summarize]]
(\cref{disjunctmax-surveys}): every uncompleted survey is missing,
\emph{regardless} of the student's grades.
We report them first with [[missing_surveys]] (\cref{surveys}) and keep them
out of the passing check, where a survey's grade would let survey
participation stand in for the examination.
Without that split, a student with a passing grade but an uncompleted survey
would be told that nothing is missing while their summarized grade is F.

One disagreement remains, and it is inherent in the policy.
A group of surveys only, with no graded assignment, summarizes to F even when
every survey is completed, since there is nothing to take the maximum of; but
there is also nothing to report as missing.
Such a group belongs with [[conjunctavg]] or [[participation]] instead.
<<helper functions>>=
def missing_assignments(assignments_list, users_list,
                        optional_assignments=None):
  """
  Returns missing assignments for disjunctive maximum grading.

  Every uncompleted survey is missing. Other assignments are only reported
  if the student has NO passing grades among them. If they have at least
  one passing grade, none of them is missing.
  """
  import re

  surveys, others = split_surveys(assignments_list)
  yield from missing_surveys(surveys, users_list, optional_assignments)

  for user in users_list:
    grades_with_assignments = []

    # First pass: collect all grades
    for assignment in others:
      # Skip optional assignments
      if optional_assignments:
        if any(re.search(opt, assignment.name) for opt in optional_assignments):
          continue

      try:
        submission = assignment.get_submission(user)
        grade = normalize_grade(submission.grade)
      except ResourceDoesNotExist:
        grade = "F"

      grades_with_assignments.append((assignment, grade))

    # Check if student has at least one passing grade (P or better)
    has_passing = any(grade_to_int(g, a) >= 0
                      for a, g in grades_with_assignments)

    if not has_passing:
      # Report all assignments as options to complete
      for assignment, grade in grades_with_assignments:
        yield user, assignment, \
              f"not a passing grade ({grade}) - complete any one to pass"
@

Both summary and missing-assignment reporting should collapse [[must fix]] to
